{"afterMs":300,"event":{"type":"agent.text.delta","payload":{"sessionId":"$SESSION","messageId":"$MSG","delta":"Here's a breakdown of your last 4 swims — there are some encouraging signs of improvement!\n\n## 📊 Performance Overview\n\n| Date | Name | Distance | Moving Time | Avg Pace (min/100m) | Avg HR | Max HR |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Apr 22 | Morning Swim | 500m | 12:18 | 2:28 | — | — |\n| Apr 29 | Morning Swim | 500m | 11:42 | 2:20 | 113.8 bpm | 147 bpm |\n| May 6 | Lunch Swim | 500m | 11:27 | 2:17 | 117.1 bpm | 138 bpm |\n| May 8 | Lunch Swim | 1000m | 26:10 | 2:37 | 106.9 bpm | 124 bpm |\n\n## ❤️ Heart Rate & Zones\n\nFor the three sessions with HR data, here's how zone time broke down:\n\n| Date | Z1 (≤120 BPM) | Z2 (121–150 BPM) | Z3+ (>150 BPM) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Apr 29 | 374s (53%) | 329s (47%) | 0s |\n| May 6 | 285s (41%) | 402s (59%) | 0s |\n| May 8 | 1516s (97%) | 54s (3%) | 0s |\n\n## 🔍 What the data says\n\n- **Pace is improving on the 500m sets**: Apr 22 → Apr 29 → May 6 you went from 2:28 → 2:20 → 2:17 per 100m — a clear and consistent upward trend.\n- **May 8's 1000m** looks slower (2:37/100m), but that's expected — it's double the distance and your first 1km session, so endurance pacing is natural.\n- **HR is trending down relative to effort**: On May 6 you held a *faster* pace than Apr 29 while your max HR dropped from 147 → 138. That's a classic sign of improving cardiovascular efficiency.\n- **May 8's HR was noticeably lower** (avg 106.9, max 124) — you kept almost entirely in Z1 throughout the 1km, which suggests you paced it conservatively (smart for a longer effort).\n- No HR data for Apr 22, so that's a gap in the comparison.\n\n**The headline:** you're getting faster at the same effort, and your heart rate ceiling is coming down — both are good indicators of genuine fitness gains. The natural next test would be a 1000m at race pace to see if that efficiency holds over the longer distance."}}}
